WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:14.310
♪ Ahhhhhh… ♪

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.890
♪ Ten years of Teams calls,
bugs and builds, ♪

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:21.150
♪ Of dashboards,
flights and endless thrills, ♪

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.380
♪ Of pull requests at half past five, ♪

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.750
♪ And pipelines somehow still alive. ♪

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.830
♪ I came, I coded, shipped some stuff, ♪

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.100
♪ Said, “One more refactor”
— that’s enough. ♪

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.080
♪ Got the crystal, got the cube, ♪

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.540
♪ And now I’m logging off for good. ♪

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.240
♪ One final commit, ♪

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.200
♪ One final deploy, ♪

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:49.060
♪ One final meeting we all could avoid… ♪

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:53.280
♪ So long, and thanks for all the tokens, ♪

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.540
♪ For every prompt and build we’ve broken, ♪

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.720
♪ For every bug that disappeared ♪

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.140
♪ As soon as someone else came near. ♪

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.440
♪ So long, and thanks for all the tokens, ♪

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.630
♪ For acronyms best left unspoken, ♪

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.840
♪ Ten years went by — somehow that’s true, ♪

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.740
♪ And now my badge is leaving too! ♪

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.650
♪ We moved to cloud, ♪

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.480
♪ then moved again, ♪

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:29.700
♪ Migrated frameworks now and then, ♪

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:36.330
♪ We added flags to hide the flags
that turned on other feature flags. ♪

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.440
♪ We queried Kusto late at night, ♪

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.910
♪ Declared the telemetry “looks alright,” ♪

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.750
♪ The build went green,
we shipped the code… ♪

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.200
♪ …then watched another incident unfold. ♪

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:52.500
♪ So long, and thanks for all the tokens, ♪

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.780
♪ For all the context windows broken, ♪

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.890
♪ Copilot said, “I found the cause!” ♪

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:02.430
♪ Then changed seventeen
files just because… ♪

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.640
♪ So long, and thanks for all the tokens, ♪

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.860
♪ For every agent we’ve awoken, ♪

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.200
♪ They planned, they reasoned,
they reviewed… ♪

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:15.080
♪ And occasionally compiled too! ♪

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:19.040
♪ There’s always one more meeting due, ♪

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:22.540
♪ One more preview to push through, ♪

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.690
♪ One more thread with forty replies, ♪

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.080
♪ And still no one knows the how or why. ♪

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.380
♪ “Quick question” never once was quick, ♪

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.880
♪ “Small change” was
rarely quite that slick, ♪

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.720
♪ And somewhere deep in A-D-O, ♪

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.820
♪ A task left from eight years ago… ♪

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:52.100
♪ But underneath the builds and on-calls, ♪

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:56.080
♪ The stand-ups, specs,
and Teams app stalls, ♪

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.760
♪ Were people I was lucky to know, ♪

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:03.500
♪ And that’s the part
that’s hard to let go. ♪

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.510
♪ I learned a lot, I built a lot, ♪

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.470
♪ I probably cached more than I ought, ♪

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.980
♪ And after ten good years, it seems ♪

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:19.000
♪ It’s time to close a few more Teams. ♪

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:22.740
♪ So long, and thanks for all the tokens, ♪

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.040
♪ For every feature built and broken, ♪

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.650
♪ Then fixed, then shipped,
then flighted wide, ♪

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.750
♪ With one last hotfix on the side. ♪

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.940
♪ So long, and thanks for all the tokens, ♪

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.220
♪ For every friendship, laugh and moment, ♪

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:45.950
♪ The final pull request is through… ♪

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.080
And if anything breaks after Tuesday…

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.520
I no longer have access.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:04:10.280
♪ SO LOOOOONG! ♪

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:11.480
♪ So… ♪

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:13.440
♪ …long! ♪
